          "title": "You'll want to know: واحة",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "واحة — wāḥa — \"an oasis\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نزلنا في واحة صغيرة في الصحراء. nazalnā fī wāḥa ṣaghīra fī aṣ-ṣaḥrāʾ. We stopped at a small oasis in the desert."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "واحة (wāḥa) was borrowed from Coptic, which goes back to ancient Egyptian (EtymDB); English oasis comes from the same word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
